{
  "kanji": "急",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 急\ntitle: urgent, sudden\njlpt: 4\ntags: [jlpt-n4, grade-3, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 9\nradical: 心\nradicalNumber: 61\nonyomi: [キュウ]\nkunyomi: [いそ.ぐ, いそ.ぎ, せ.く]\ndistractors: [悪, 思, 色]\n---\n\n# 急 — urgent, sudden\n\n**Strokes:** 9 · **Key (radical):** 心 (heart, no. 61) · **JLPT:** N4 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n急 connects hurrying, urgency, and sudden change. It can also describe a steep slope, so not every use is about a person rushing.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** picture the angular shapes above [心](心.md) pressing down on a heart that feels hurried. This is a modern visual memory aid, not an origin claim.\n\n## Readings\n\nThis table is selective; metadata preserves all source on/kun readings.\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| キュウ | on | 急に きゅうに (suddenly), 急行 きゅうこう (express train) |\n| いそ.ぐ | kun | [急ぐ](../words/急ぐ.md) いそぐ (hurry) |\n| いそ.ぎ | kun | 急ぎ いそぎ (haste; urgency), 急ぎ足 いそぎあし (a quick pace), お急ぎ おいそぎ (in a hurry) |\n| せ.く | kun | 急く せく (to hurry; to be impatient), 気が急く きがせく (feel impatient), 急いては事を仕損じる せいてはことをしそんじる (haste makes waste) |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [急ぐ](../words/急ぐ.md) いそぐ — hurry\n- 急に きゅうに — suddenly\n- 急行 きゅうこう — express train\n- 急用 きゅうよう — urgent business\n\n## Notes\n\n急な坂 きゅうなさか means \"a steep slope\"; 急な changes a following noun. 急に often describes how an event happens, as in 急に雨が降った きゅうにあめがふった (it suddenly started raining).\n\nCompare the upper shapes of 急, [悪](悪.md), and [思](思.md): they all end in 心 but are separate characters with different readings.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-08 (EDRDG; [CC BY-SA 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)).\n",
